   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "REDRAW ONLY THE PART YOU PAINT; every other pixel of the frame stays exactly as it was (no drift).\n\n1. Flatten the frame first:  python tools/comfyui/prep_frame.py <frame.png>  (puts it on the grey background the LoRA was trained on; writes <frame>_flat.png).\n2. Load it in 'Frame to fix', right-click > Open in MaskEditor, paint over the part to redraw (a hand, the face, a ribbon). Paint a bit past the edges.\n3. Say what should be there in the prompt (after the trigger word).\n4. Queue (4 tries). 'Masked area' shows what will change.\n5. cutout.py on the result, like a new pose.\n\nToo little change: denoise 0.7. Too much / off-model: denoise 0.4. Seam visible: grow mask 12."
   ],
   "title": "READ ME: Netsu VS fix a frame",
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
